2. \( T = 2\pi \sqrt{\frac{r^3}{GM}} \)

From these equations, we can see that if the speed decreases, the radius must also decrease to maintain the balance of forces. Consequently, the period of revolution will also change. Specifically, as the radius decreases, the period will decrease as well, since \( T \) is proportional to \( r^{3/2} \).

